  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 11, the Risk workflow — a risk-and-opportunity classifier. It receives trend, sentiment and metrics data, validates payloads and schema, initialises a run context, loads classifier config (thresholds, weights, labels) and domain rules, preprocesses signals by normalising scales and handling missing values, builds feature vectors per entity or trend, and computes a risk score and an opportunity score. Two threshold gateways follow — \"Risk score above risk_threshold?\" tagging risk_candidate or not_risk_candidate, then \"Opportunity score above opportunity_threshold?\" tagging opportunity_candidate or not — after which a final label is derived from {risk, opportunity, mixed, neutral}. A materiality gateway assigns LOW priority or HIGH/MEDIUM, and the run builds and persists a risk_opportunity record with scores, labels and reasons. This is the workflow on which Figure 3 shows the specialist system's largest advantage.",
